tasks.prompt:
You are given the following JSON document describing school bus routes:

```json
{
  "routes": [
    {"name": "North", "stops": [
      {"name": "Elm", "students": 12},
      {"name": "Oak", "students": 8},
      {"name": "Pine", "students": 15}
    ]},
    {"name": "South", "stops": [
      {"name": "Maple", "students": 10},
      {"name": "Cedar", "students": 7}
    ]},
    {"name": "East", "stops": []}
  ]
}
```

Write a program that produces the following output, exactly:

```
North: 3 stops, 35 students, busiest Oak
South: 2 stops, 17 students, busiest Maple
East: 0 stops, 0 students, no stops
All routes: 5 stops, 52 students
```

For each route (in document order), print `Name: ` the number of stops, ` stops, ` the total students, `, busiest ` the name of the stop with the most students (if there is a tie, the first one in document order), or the literal `no stops` if the route has no stops. The last line prints `All routes: ` the total stops across all routes, ` stops, ` the total students across all routes, ` students`. No trailing spaces on any line.

A beekeeper records hive sensor readings as a JSON document. Flatten each hive record into a single line of dot-separated key paths.

The JSON document contains the following hives:

```json
{
  "hives": [
    {
      "tag": "H1",
      "sensors": { "temp_c": 34.2, "humidity": 61, "weight_kg": 42.8 },
      "queen": { "marked": true, "year": 2023 }
    },
    {
      "tag": "H2",
      "sensors": { "temp_c": 33.7, "humidity": 58, "weight_kg": 39.1 },
      "queen": { "marked": false, "year": 2024 }
    },
    {
      "tag": "H3",
      "sensors": { "temp_c": 35.1, "humidity": 64, "weight_kg": 47.5 },
      "queen": { "marked": true, "year": 2022 }
    }
  ]
}
```

Print one line per hive in document order:

`<tag> | sensors.temp_c=<v>; sensors.humidity=<v>; sensors.weight_kg=<v>; queen.marked=<v>; queen.year=<v>`

- Reals print with exactly 1 decimal place (e.g. `34.2`).
- Ints print without a decimal point.
- Bools print as `true` or `false`.
- Text prints as-is.

After all hive lines print one summary line:

`avg_temp=<mean of all sensors.temp_c to 2 decimal places>`

No value is exactly halfway when rounded. There are no trailing spaces. Output exactly 4 lines.

A board game club stores match results as a JSON document. Flatten each match into a single line of dot-separated key paths.

The JSON document contains the following matches:

```json
{
  "matches": [
    {
      "game": "Catan",
      "players": [
        { "name": "Ana", "score": 10 },
        { "name": "Ben", "score": 7 }
      ],
      "duration_min": 78,
      "winner": "Ana"
    },
    {
      "game": "Azul",
      "players": [
        { "name": "Cleo", "score": 55 },
        { "name": "Dev", "score": 61 }
      ],
      "duration_min": 42,
      "winner": "Dev"
    },
    {
      "game": "Ticket to Ride",
      "players": [
        { "name": "Eli", "score": 120 },
        { "name": "Fay", "score": 95 }
      ],
      "duration_min": 96,
      "winner": "Eli"
    }
  ]
}
```

Print one line per match in document order:

`<game> | players.0.name=<v>; players.0.score=<v>; players.1.name=<v>; players.1.score=<v>; duration_min=<v>; winner=<v>`

- Text prints as-is (no quotes).
- Ints print without a decimal point.
- Bools print as `true` or `false`.

After all match lines print one summary line:

`longest=<game name of the match with the highest duration_min, ties broken by document order>`

There are no trailing spaces. Output exactly 4 lines.
